  "steps": [
    "Heat the oven to 400°F and line a large rimmed baking sheet with parchment.",
    "Whisk the dressing ingredients together and set aside.",
    "Put the lentils, tomatoes, bell pepper, eggplant, onion, gnocchi and chopped garlic on the pan. Drizzle with the dressing and toss until everything is well coated. Spread in an even layer.",
    "Roast 25 minutes, tossing at the 15-minute mark, until the gnocchi are golden and the eggplant is tender.",
    "Crumble the goat cheese over the top and roast 5 minutes more, until softened.",
    "Serve right away, topped with the herbs, a drizzle of olive oil and the olives if using."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Vacuum-packed shelf-stable gnocchi crisp best; there is no need to boil them first.",
    "Cut all the vegetables the same size so they finish together.",
    "Chickpeas, butter beans or cannellini can replace the lentils, and shrimp or chicken can be added.",
    "Keeps 4 days in the fridge. Reheat at 375°F for 5-7 minutes, or eat it cold as a pasta salad."
  ],
